  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We have to find the area of the region&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#8804;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Now, to find the point of intersection of the curves&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we equate the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;to get</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mfenced><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;or&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>And, the graph of the given functions is as</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/55ab0f66-2ac5-432b-8e18-f7c112d82f48-image.png\" style=\"width: 210px; height: 223px;\" /></p><p>The shaded area is the required area, and&nbsp;</p><p>Area<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>n</mi><mi>e</mi></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>r</mi><mi>a</mi><mi>b</mi><mi>o</mi><mi>l</mi><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mo>&#8747;</mo><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></math></p><p>Now, using&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8747;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;we get</p><p>Area<math><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>y</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mrow><mn>6</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msubsup></math></p><p><math><mo>=</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>32</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math>&nbsp;sq units.</p>",
